# Line endings are LF in the repository *and* in every working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with the default `core.autocrlf=true` — which
# is what the GitHub Windows runner uses — converts LF to CRLF on checkout, and
# Biome's `lineEnding: "lf"` then reports every single file as unformatted. That
# is a real failure the Windows CI leg caught on the first run; `eol=lf` is the
# fix, rather than relaxing the formatter.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary

# Generated; keep it out of diffs and reviews without making it untracked.
package-lock.json   -diff linguist-generated=true
